                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6e6b0be5-548c-3eeb-b2a3-36315b1db832",
                        "entry_id": "9fcd28ff-24fc-37d0-8523-3a9812ee11bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A malignant tumor that arises in the lymph nodes or in other lymphoid tissue."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6e888a6-f3e8-4872-a1ca-23d4a06079a0",
                                "sense_id": "6e6b0be5-548c-3eeb-b2a3-36315b1db832",
                                "text": "In the one sub-class, we have the Leukaemic Lymphoma, the Typhous Lymphoma, the Hyperplastic Lymphoma (ex. the simple hypertrophied tonsil), Lympho-sarcoma, Scrofulous Glands; and in the other sub-class, Tubercle of man, and Perlsucht or Parresyge, or Morbus Gallicus, the pearl distemper of ruminating animals."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a348cc6-4a7d-4155-bcbe-aa6aef1cb2ad",
                                "sense_id": "6e6b0be5-548c-3eeb-b2a3-36315b1db832",
                                "text": "Common immunohistochemical markers of this lymphoma include CD2, CD56, CD3, and T-cell receptors. 7 Typically, the histology of these lymphomas are characterized by monomorphic inflammatory cellular infiltrates, which may be diffuse or show angiocentricity and angiodestruction as well as tissue destruction. 7 Lymphoid markers from the nasal mucosal biopsy from this patient were negative for CD56 and EBER."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
